      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 164.93,
      "end_seconds": 169.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.91,
      "text": "a a few quick ones: heartburn, coughing up blood or weight loss?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 171.09,
      "end_seconds": 176.11,
      "duration_seconds": 5.02,
      "text": "No no heartburn coughing up blood or weight loss."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 176.63,
      "end_seconds": 179.5,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "yes, carry on. Neurologically, anything strange?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 181.1,
      "end_seconds": 182.61,
      "duration_seconds": 1.51,
      "text": "nothing odd there"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 196.38,
      "end_seconds": 199.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "I'll note down your vital signs first"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 210.93,
      "end_seconds": 213.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "So that's it just a little longer..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 225.8,
      "end_seconds": 233.56,
      "duration_seconds": 7.76,
      "text": "Okay: SpO2 97 percent on room air, BP is 120 over 68, respiratory rate 16, pulse 69."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 235.32,
      "end_seconds": 237.0,
      "duration_seconds": 1.68,
      "text": "is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.51,
      "end_seconds": 240.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "we'll look at it together shortly"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 242.74,
      "end_seconds": 246.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "I'll examine you in a second, make yourself comfortable"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 248.06,
      "end_seconds": 249.83,
      "duration_seconds": 1.77,
      "text": "Let me feel here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 267.77,
      "end_seconds": 272.2,
      "duration_seconds": 4.43,
      "text": "your chest is clear and there is no wheeze"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 277.68,
      "end_seconds": 291.67,
      "duration_seconds": 13.99,
      "text": "all finished thank you taking everything into account I don't have a clear answer today: a persistent dry cough without a clear cause so far is possible and so is reflux"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 292.34,
      "end_seconds": 295.59,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "Do you think it's something serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 299.89,
      "end_seconds": 337.18,
      "duration_seconds": 37.29,
      "text": "I understand the worry at the moment I'd say it's a persistent dry cough without a clear cause so far, and we'll know more once the a chest X-ray is back i'm sending you for a chest X-ray because of chronic cough we will review your tablets and see whether the cough settles over a a month the thing that would worry me is if you cough up blood or lose weight if that happens, go to emergency"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 342.62,
      "end_seconds": 345.76,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "okay, I'll look out for that"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 346.83,
      "end_seconds": 349.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "we'll catch up in six weeks"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 350.54,
      "end_seconds": 352.52,
      "duration_seconds": 1.98,
      "text": "alright, I'll be back"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 354.52,
      "end_seconds": 358.93,
      "duration_seconds": 4.41,
      "text": "Right, that's the plan. Do you wanna ask me anything?"
    },
